#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0899 expect=noViolation domain=ADSL
#note "EC-43 boundary: JOIN SHADOWING, not the fold. ADSL carries no RFSTDTC column while DM does. ExprCompiler.nameRefPlan resolves an unqualified name against the primary table, then against any Match_Datasets join, and ONLY THEN folds an absent column to all-missing - so the unqualified RFSTDTC resolves to the joined DM column, compares equal to DM.RFSTDTC, and nothing is reported. Same contract as BroadcastFoldTest.joinedDatasetSurfaceableColumnDoesNotFold. If nameRefPlan ever folds before consulting the join, this scenario goes red and 9 rules turn live. Paired with CDISC-AD0899-invalid-ADSL.cdt so it cannot pass vacuously."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADSL class=ADSL label="Subject Level Analysis Dataset"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SAFFL   type=Char label="Safety Population Flag"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | Y
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | Y
---

dataset DM class="SPECIAL PURPOSE" label="Demographics"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col RFSTDTC type=Char label="Subject Reference Start Date/Time"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1015 | 2013-01-04
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1023 | 2012-08-05
---
